temp_media/
tmp.md
tmp/
downloads/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# server/invite_roster.json IS tracked (git-authoritative roster, split
# from the old server-only invites.json 2026-08-12 — see server/README.md).
# Only the live per-slug status data stays server-only, and that file
# (invite_status.json) never touches this repo in the first place.

# Generated build output (PDFs, assembled markdown, LaTeX preamble,
# rendered website). Both the Mac and the server independently rebuild
# these from source — tracking them in git means whichever side commits
# last blocks the other side's `git pull` on its own uncommitted local
# rebuild (see build/atomic_sanskrit.trade.short.pdf history for the
# conflict this caused 2026-08-11). Regenerate with build_book.py /
# build_html.py; never commit build/ output again.
build/

# Secrets. hypothesis/token.txt has its own hypothesis/.gitignore entry;
# these cover the server/ side and any future *_token.txt / *_api_token.txt
# dropped anywhere in the tree. A Hypothesis personal API token is
# unscoped and never expires, so one committed by accident is a full
# account compromise that survives in history until the token is revoked.
*token.txt
*_api_token.txt
server/*.token
